=Jong-Han Kim - Biography

== Education 

- Ph.D. in [http://aa.stanford.edu Aeronautics and Astronautics], [http://www.stanford.edu Stanford University] (2012) \n
	[http://isl.stanford.edu /Information Systems Lab./]
- M.S. in [http://ae.kaist.ac.kr Aerospace Engineering], [http://www.kaist.ac.kr Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology (KAIST)] (2001) \n
	[http://fdcl.kaist.ac.kr /Flight Dynamics and Control Lab./]
- B.S. in [http://ae.kaist.ac.kr Aerospace Engineering], [http://www.kaist.ac.kr Korea Advanced Institute of Science and Technology (KAIST)] (1999)

== Work Experience
- Associate Professor, [http://aerospace.inha.ac.kr Department of Aerospace Engineering], [http://www.inha.ac.kr Inha University] (2022-)
- Assistant Professor, [http://aerospace.inha.ac.kr Department of Aerospace Engineering], [http://www.inha.ac.kr Inha University] (2021-2022)
- Assistant Professor, [http://ee.khu.ac.kr Department of Electronic Engineering], [http://www.khu.ac.kr Kyung Hee University] (2018-2021)
- Senior Researcher, [http://www.add.re.kr Agency for Defense Development (ADD)], Republic of Korea (2001-2018)


== Honors and Awards

- Best Paper Award (Student Paper, Guidance, Navigation, and Control Technical Committee), /American Institute of Aeronautics and Astronautics (AIAA)/, 2026. \n
/For the paper [https://arc.aiaa.org/doi/10.2514/6.2026-1169 Neural Projection Operators for Real-Time 6-DoF Powered Descent Guidance], presented at the 2026 AIAA SciTech Forum./

- Outstanding Paper Presentation Award, /Korean Society for Aeronautical and Space Sciences (KSAS)/, 2026. \n
/For the paper [https://www.dbpia.co.kr/journal/articleDetail?nodeId=NODE12757864 Intervention Learning-Based Safe Reinforcement Learning Using Control Barrier Functions], presented at the 2026 KSAS Spring Conference./

- Outstanding Paper Presentation Award, /Korean Society for Aeronautical and Space Sciences (KSAS)/, 2026. \n
/For the paper [https://www.dbpia.co.kr/journal/articleDetail?nodeId=NODE12589768 Angle-of-Attack Estimation Using a PINN-Based Observer], presented at the 2025 KSAS Fall Conference./ 

- Outstanding Paper Presentation Award, /Korean Society for Aeronautical and Space Sciences (KSAS)/, 2025. \n
/For the paper [https://www.dbpia.co.kr/journal/articleDetail?nodeId=NODE12061201 Powered Descent Guidance via Neural Network Based Projection Operator], present at the 2024 KSAS Fall Conference/

- Commendation from the Minister of National Defense, /Republic of Korea/, 2017. \n
/In recognition of pivotal roles in applying machine learning and convex optimization techniques for developing cutting-edge missile guidance systems./ 

- Outstanding Young Researcher Award, /Institute of Control, Robotics and Systems (ICROS)/, 2017. \n
/Given to outstanding young researchers under 40 with notable research achievements./
